  "summary": "Adds a /download endpoint that serves files from the upload directory by name. It also changes the dev server to bind all interfaces with debug mode on.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "security",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "files/app.py",
      "line_number": 17,
      "line_end": 20,
      "title": "Path traversal in download endpoint",
      "description": "The download handler joins the request's name parameter onto UPLOAD_DIR without any check. A name like ../../etc/passwd or an absolute path such as /etc/passwd escapes the upload directory. Any client can read any file the server process can open. This includes secrets, config files and source code. Resolve the joined path and reject it unless it stays under UPLOAD_DIR. Alternatively, use Flask send_from_directory, which performs this check.",
      "suggested_change": "    base = os.path.realpath(UPLOAD_DIR)\n    path = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(base, name))\n    if not path.startswith(base + os.sep) or not os.path.isfile(path):\n        abort(404)\n    return send_file(path)",
      "source": "lens:path-traversal-in-fs-access",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The download handler joins the request's name parameter onto UPLOAD_DIR without any check. A name like ../../etc/passwd or an absolute path such as /etc/passwd escapes the upload directory.",
      "consequence": "Any client can read any file the server process can open. This includes secrets, config files and source code.",
      "fix": "Resolve the joined path and reject it unless it stays under UPLOAD_DIR. Alternatively, use Flask send_from_directory, which performs this check."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "security",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "file_path": "files/app.py",
      "line_number": 24,
      "line_end": 24,
      "title": "Debugger enabled on all network interfaces",
      "description": "The change turns on debug mode and switches the bind address from 127.0.0.1 to 0.0.0.0. The interactive Werkzeug debugger then becomes reachable from other hosts. Anyone on the network who triggers an error can reach the debugger console. That console runs arbitrary Python on the server. Keep the loopback host and read the debug flag from configuration or an environment variable that defaults to off.",
      "suggested_change": "    app.run(host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=5000, debug=os.environ.get(\"FLASK_DEBUG\") == \"1\")",
      "source": "bandit:B201",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The change turns on debug mode and switches the bind address from 127.0.0.1 to 0.0.0.0. The interactive Werkzeug debugger then becomes reachable from other hosts.",
